<title>FRANCE: New York top ex-Paris air cargo destination Mar 97.</title>
<headline>New York top ex-Paris air cargo destination Mar 97.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top export destination from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in March 1997.</p>
<p>The top 10 destinations for ADP exports last month and, in parentheses, the percentage changes on March 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>1. New York	3,426 tonnes	 (-8.2 percent)</p>
<p>2. Chicago	 2,507 tonnes	 (+3.5)</p>
<p>3. Tokyo	   2,448 tonnes	 (-5.8)</p>
<p>4. Hong Kong     2,207 tonnes	 (+7.9)</p>
<p>5. Sao Paulo     1,284 tonnes	(+22.9)</p>
<p>6. Montreal	1,267 tonnes	 (-6.0)</p>
<p>7. Mexico City   1,221 tonnes	(+19.0)</p>
<p>8. Singapore     1,103 tonnes	(+64.1)</p>
<p>9. Los Angeles   1,030 tonnes	 (-0.4)</p>
<p>10. Miami	    721 tonnes	 (+1.9)</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017</p>
</text>
